RF.put("questb:b56",{"8696":{"id":8696,"t":"Cloak of the Unseen Path","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Regal Drape, 2 Lambent Idols, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Keyl Swiftclaw in Silithus. You must also obtain Revered reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Regal Drape General Rajaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Kurinnaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Lambent Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 21000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"I'm glad to hear you're aiding us in our attack on Ahn'Qiraj, ‹name›. I can make you a protective item that'll be of assistance in the fight against our enemy, ‹class›.\nI shall need a Qiraji drape, which I'll resize for you of course. I'll also need idols and scarabs which I'll use to create a suitable clasp.\nI promise you won't be disappointed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCloak of the Unseen Path\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring the materials for the cloak, ‹name›?","done":"Ah yes... this drape is immaculate.\nTake this cloak, ‹name›. May it protect you from the foul magic of the Qiraji.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.8,"y":39.5,"n":"Keyl Swiftclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8616":{"id":8616,"t":"The Horde Needs More Baked Salmon!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Baked Salmon to Chief Sharpclaw at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Baked Salmon","desc":"The last batch of baked salmon that you donated to the war effort looked very delicious, ‹class›. I must admit that I was tempted to take a few for myself. As you can tell, we have not yet reached our quota here. I am hoping you have returned because you have another stack of baked salmon with you","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":28.8,"y":68.4,"n":"Chief Sharpclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"696":{"id":696,"t":"Attack on the Tower","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Trelane's Phylactery, Trelane's Orb, and Trelane's Ember Agate, and return them to Skuerto at Refuge Pointe.\nTrelane's Phylactery Trelane's Footlocker\nTrelane's Orb Trelane's Lockbox\nTrelane's Ember Agate Trelane's Chest","desc":"Here's what your lookin' for: Trelane's phylactery, Trelane's orb, an' Trelane's ember agate.\nAll three should be in chests within the tower an' you shouldn't have a problem opening the chests on your own; you just have to be careful of the ogres.\nThe tower's defenses won't take care of 'em on their own; you'll need to have your weapons at the ready. Those ogres find out you're there and stealing from 'em, an' they'll be sure to put the hurt on you.\nBe careful, an' good luck.","rew":"Experience: 3,000\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"You do this, an' I'm sure Malin'll be more than pleased with you.","done":"Malin couldn't've asked a worthier person to come here an' aid us, ‹name›. You've done a grand job!\nHe'll be pleased to see what an overwhelming success our mission's been.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46.7,"y":47,"n":"Skuerto","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"216":{"id":216,"t":"Between a Rock and a Thistlefur","lv":24,"min":21,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take down 8 Thistlefur Avengers and 8 Thistlefur Shaman; most are located east of Zoram Strand in Thistlefur Village. Once completed, return to Karang Amakkar at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.\nThistlefur Avenger slain : 0/ 8\nThistlefur Shaman slain : 0/ 8","desc":"The Thistlefur furbolgs are threatening our expansion! Thistlefur Village to our east blocks the way between us here and the Splintertree Post. It's a path that would circumvent the village of Astranaar; without it, we give the Alliance an extra expansion path.\n‹name›, we must not allow... an expansion path gap!\nProceed to Thistlefur Village and thin out the furbolgs. You will be given compensation for this task, but more importantly you will be doing your duty for the Horde!","rew":"Money: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Have you taken the fight to the Thistlefur? With a clear path between our bases, our chances of claiming the whole of Ashenvale increase dramatically.","done":"Well done ‹class›, well done! I will continue to send forces to thin out the furbolg, but I can at least count on a different path that will be free of Alliance entanglements. The Horde conquest of Ashenvale is now in full swing!\nYou've earned your pay this day, hero. I salute you!","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":11.9,"y":34.5,"n":"Karang Amakkar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1016":{"id":1016,"t":"Elemental Bracers","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 5 Intact Elemental Bracers and use the Divining Scroll on them. Afterwards, bring the Divined Scroll to Sentinel Velene Starstrike at the Silverwind Refuge.\nDivined Scroll\nProvided: Divining Scroll","desc":"Take this divining scroll--it can determine the creator of these elementals. But you will need something from them to use as a reagent to focus scroll's magic--their bracers should do nicely.\nA few intact bracers from the creatures should be enough. The other bracers will be useless for our purposes, but they may be worth something to a merchant if you wish to sell them. Once you have the intact bracers attempt to use the scroll. Return to me with the results and we shall proceed from there.","rew":"Experience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Since you must destroy the bracers to kill the elementals, it will probably be difficult to find the specific ones that contain the information the divining scroll needs. You can trade bracers with others in order to obtain the ones you need, or perhaps you have the divined paper already?","done":"Well done, ‹name›, this should give us the information we need to have the culprit discovered. How would you feel about taking out the mage who fills our pools with corrupt elementals? The corruption of Ashenvale and beyond makes my stomach turn on its own--to have a wizard actively attempting to destroy it further sickens me to no end. We shall make him pay.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":49.8,"y":67.2,"n":"Sentinel Velene Starstrike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"4136":{"id":4136,"t":"Ribbly Screwspigot","lv":53,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ribbly's Head to Yuka Screwspigot in the Burning Steppes.\nRibbly's Head Ribbly Screwspigot","desc":"My brother Ribbly has always been a drain to his family, taking our money and wasting it on one scheme after another.\nWell, his last scheme must have been his worst, because Baron Revilgaz of Booty Bay just put a price on poor Ribbly's head. I can't tell you how happy this makes the Screwspigots! Our little Ribbly's finally worth something!\nBut now he's hiding out, deep in Blackrock Depths. Please, find him and bring him to me!\nOr, if he won't come, then that's ok... just bring me his head.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRancor Boots Penance Spaulders Splintsteel Armor\nMoney: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650","back":"Do you have Ribbly? Or, at least a part of him?","done":"Aha! You found him! And... it appears that my little brother didn't want to come quiety. It's a pity. I would have liked to see the look on his face when I told him our plans to turn him in to Revilgaz.\nThank you, ‹name›. You've made my family very happy. And Ribbly's never looked as peaceful as he does now.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":66.1,"y":22,"n":"Yuka Screwspigot","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"7656":{"id":7656,"t":"Imperial Plate Chest","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Thorium Bar","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Imperial Plate Chest\n+200 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"For the chest piece plans, I'll be needin' 60 thorium bars.\nOh boy, there you go again. Are you gonna be runnin' to yer blue Gods, askin' why they have forsaken you?!? Toughen up, Nancy! Nobody ever said life's fair.","done":"A pleasure doin' business with ya.\nAnd ‹name›, wipe that look of disgust off yer face.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.7,"n":"Derotain Mudsipper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"4296":{"id":4296,"t":"Tablet of the Seven","lv":50,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Tablet Transcript to Maxwort Uberglint in the Burning Steppes.\nTablet Transcript","desc":"I came to the Burning Steppes, following the legends of the Seven. They were dwarves of great knowledge and power, and if you have knowledge and power, then wealth is sure to follow.\nThat's what I want. Wealth!\nIf we can learn more of the Seven, then maybe we can get rich together. The ruins of Thaurissan is rumored to keep the Tablet of the Seven, which holds knowledge of the ancient dwarves. Find this tablet, copy its text and bring it to me. Let's discover its secrets together!","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,350","back":"Do you have the writings of the Seven, ‹name›? Have you learned the secrets from their tablet?","done":"Ah, you found the tablet! And your transcription is superb! Are you sure you're a ‹class› and not a scribe?\nHere you are, ‹name›. Here is the payment I promised.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65.2,"y":23.9,"n":"Maxwort Uberglint","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"96056":{"id":96056,"t":"Camping 101 skinning","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Balthus Stoneflayer in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your skinning skill to 20","desc":"Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Camp Chair. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nDun Morogh Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Eric Brighthammer","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":39.6,"y":32.4,"n":"Balthus Stoneflayer","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"92456":{"id":92456,"t":"A green sample","lv":33,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect a Fel Infused Blossom from the City of Dalaran for Shylamiir in Stormwind City.\nFel Infused Blossom","desc":"If you're going to bother me you can at least make yourself useful. I have an errand I need run.\nFor a city of mages, Dalaran has a surprising interest in botany. The Kirin Tor keep to themselves, but I would love a sample of their mana-infused vegetation.\nYou're clearly someone who is comfortable being where people don't want you, maybe you could find a way into the city. If you do, bring me back whatever is growing in their central garden.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nVine Pruner's Cloak Thorn Protecting Girdle\nExperience: 9,400\nLevel 33 , requires level 24 Difficulty 24 29 31 36 42 Side Alliance Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 92456","cats":["city-of-dalaran"]},"94216":{"id":94216,"t":"Craftsmans writ elixir of lesser agility","min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Elixir of Lesser Agility\nElixir of Lesser Agility","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Elixir of Lesser Agility, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Are you here about...\n<Ziz looks around his tiny hut suspiciously, and lowers his voice.>\nThe elixir?","done":"<Ziz continues to talk in a hushed tone.>\nI'm not about to give you the whole spiel about how I got into this position, but here's some advice for you.\nSometimes, all you gotta do to impress your new boss is take credit for someone else's work. So you're going to hand over the elixir, and I am gonna talk about how much blood, sweat, and tears I poured into making it.\nIt's a new gig, okay? I need to make a good first impression!","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59,"y":62.6,"n":"Ziz Fizziks","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94296":{"id":94296,"t":"Craftsmans writ wild leather shoulders","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Wild Leather Shoulders\nWild Leather Shoulders","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Wild Leather Shoulders, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Wild Leather Shoulders Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94296","cats":["crafting"]},"7896":{"id":7896,"t":"Green Fireworks","lv":60,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"36 Green Firework sold by Ziggle Sparks , sold by Wizbang Booms , sold by Lillian Singh , sold by Jaxxil Sparks and 3 more","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"When I finally get this booth up and running, I'll want to advertise! And what better way is there to advertise than with fireworks?\nWell, some might think that the smell of a cauldron, churning with the boiling heads of your foes is better for drawing crowds, but... we're in mixed company. So fireworks it will have to be!\nBring me green fireworks, ‹name›, and I have a big fistful of Darkmoon Faire tickets for you.","done":"You brought the fireworks. Wonderful work, ‹name›! I can't wait to light these and tell the world that my booth is ready to go! I must still wait, quite a long time I'm afraid, but... I'll be ready when I'm ready, yes?\nHere are the tickets, ‹name›. Enjoy yourself!\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38,"y":44.3,"n":"Rinling","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.7,"y":70.7,"n":"Rinling","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"56":{"id":56,"t":"The Night Watch","lv":24,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke of Darkshire wants you to kill 8 Skeletal Warriors and 6 Skeletal Mages.\nSkeletal Warrior slain : 0/ 8\nSkeletal Mage slain : 0/ 6","desc":"As Commander of The Night Watch it is my sworn duty to protect the citizens of Darkshire. Stormwind has retracted their commissioned guards from their posts here, leaving us to our own devices.\nIf you feel worthy of the task, we need your help! Assist The Night Watch by venturing forth into Tranquil Gardens, just south of Darkshire, and slaying 8 Skeletal Warriors and 6 Skeletal Mages. The undead threat must be thwarted!","rew":"Money: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,450\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you killed those warriors and mages?","done":"Splendid, ‹name›. For your service to the people of Darkshire you shall be rewarded.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.5,"y":46.8,"n":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"6136":{"id":6136,"t":"The Corpulent One","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Borelgore in the northern wastes of Eastern Plaguelands and destroy him. Return to Nathanos Blightcaller when the mission is complete.\nBorelgore slain","desc":"Past the Argent Dawn encampment of Light's Hope and west of Northdale, you will find the corpulent maggot beast, Borelgore.\nI've lost entire regiments to that monster. His size knows no bounds! The more he eats the greater his girth becomes...\nWhile I would not suffer any emotional harm should the beast devour you, I would prefer that you were the victor. Borelgore has been known to devour others who tried to hunt him.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nIchor Spitter Skullstone Hammer Sarah's Guide\nMoney: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have I told you lately that I hate you?","done":"Keep this up and I may have to promote you from imbecile to mental deficient, first class.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.2,"y":63.5,"n":"Nathanos Blightcaller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"91736":{"id":91736,"t":"Applejack still","min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"4 Shiny Red Apple","rew":"You will receive:\nThunder Applejack","back":"A strong scent of apples burns your nose as you inspect the device.\nShiny Red Apple (4)","done":"The machine dispenses a clear liquid into a bottle...","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":24.5,"y":58.2,"n":"Applejack Still","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"536":{"id":536,"t":"Down the Coast","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Torn Fin Tidehunters and 10 Torn Fin Oracles for Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore.\nTorn Fin Tidehunter slain : 0/ 10\nTorn Fin Oracle slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Transferred from the Stormwind city guard to Southshore, a town that should be abandoned by the looks of it... Smell of the harbor day and night.\nNot to mention ol' Redpath... Wants me to take care of the murlocs. Ha!\nI can barely rouse myself to go out to some of the pockets of the overgrown fish down the Western Strand. If you would go in my place and take care of them, I'd appreciate it.","rew":"Money: 21 0 gold, 21 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,850","back":"Another ale, please, the last one just seemed to have disappeared!\nLight, how much longer am I going to be stuck out here?\nOh, it's you, ‹name›. Have you killed those murlocs yet?","done":"I hope this will be enough to convince Redpath that I've--ha!--been carrying out his orders and ridding Southshore of the terrible and horrible menace of the dreaded murlocs! For there could be no greater evil than the ravages of overgrown fish!","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.5,"y":58.4,"n":"Lieutenant Farren Orinelle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"9336":{"id":9336,"t":"Major Healing Potion","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0.","obj":"15 Necrotic Rune Bone Witch , Spirit of the Damned , Lumbering Horror , Shadow of Doom 38.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nMajor Healing Potion","back":"In addition to our other supplies, we also have a number of major healing potions you may find useful. I will give you one in exchange for fifteen necrotic runes.","done":"Here you are, ‹name›. Be careful out there. Our numbers are not so large we can afford many battlefield casualties.\nUndercity Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":65,"y":45.6,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.2,"y":73.8,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":42.1,"y":58.5,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"8936":{"id":8936,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Dreadmist Belt and a set of Dreadmist Wraps to Deliana in Ironforge.\nDreadmist Belt Scholomance Necromancer 1.7 % in Scholomance , Thuzadin Shadowcaster 1.3 % in Stratholme , Thuzadin Necromancer 1.2 % in Stratholme , Crimson Conjuror 0.9 % in Stratholme and 1 more\nDreadmist Wraps Lorekeeper Polkelt 17 % in Scholomance , Scholomance Necromancer 0 % in Scholomance","desc":"You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me the belt and set of gloves that you wish to upgrade. I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathmist Belt Deathmist Wraps\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the trade?","done":"You've kept your end of the bargain, I shall keep mine.\nJust remember that I'm holding on to the best pieces until your work is finished.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2856":{"id":2856,"t":"Wild Leather Vest","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Turtle Scale Breastplates, 2 Turtle Scale Gloves, and a Wildvine to Jangdor Swiftstrider in Camp Mojache.\n2 Turtle Scale Breastplate\n2 Turtle Scale Gloves\nWildvine Retherokk the Berserker 80.6 % , Zul'arek Hatefowler 65.1 % , Purple Lotus 10 % , Vilebranch Aman'zasi Guard 9.5 % and 4 more","desc":"Wild Leather vests are the staple of any Wild Leather armor set. The frame of the vest and the wildvine weave within it produces a product that offers maximum protection of the torso while allowing for potent magic to work its way through the garment.\nFor this pattern, I will require two Turtle Scale breastplates, two sets of Turtle Scale gloves, and a wildvine. This is not an easy lesson, but it is one you certainly have the skill to complete.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Wild Leather Vest\nExperience: 2,900","back":"Do you have the two Turtle Scale breastplates and gloves? Also, don't forget the wildvine!\nEven with the earliest patterns, we learn that the fundamentals of shape translate well into more difficult garments. Though different items, the shape of the Turtle Scale breastplates prepares you for the detailing needed to make a Wild Leather vest.\nAs you progress through your lessons, the skills I teach will become as art.","done":"These are some very nice pieces here, ‹name›. The craftsmanship and care put in to making these show you have chosen to dedicate yourself fully to these tasks.\nYou've met my requests, and with that comes your reward. The knowledge of making Wild Leather vests is now yours!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":42.9,"n":"Jangdor Swiftstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"86776":{"id":86776,"t":"Ingredients for the forge","lv":30,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 10 Bronze Bars to Morhan Coppertongue.\n10 Bronze Bar","desc":"Thelsamar's a great place to live, but we don't have all of the amenities of Ironforge. I'm always running out of bronze! I need more bronze if I'm going to keep making tools and kettles and pots!\nI can tell you have a little experience at the forge. Think you could smelt me some bronze bars? I can pay you well for it!","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Tin Bar\nMoney: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Gotta keep the forges going!","done":"Ah, this is a relief! I should be able to keep the forge going now. Hopefully one of these days we'll get a trader bringing coal into town regularly!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":34,"y":46.6,"n":"Morhan Coppertongue","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"1656":{"id":1656,"t":"A Task Unfinished","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Bundle of Furs to Innkeeper Kauth in Bloodhoof Village.\nBundle of Furs\nProvided: Bundle of Furs","desc":"‹name›, please, I beg of you, can you help me? I have not finished my tasks here on the Mesa--I'm in the middle of my Rite of Strength--and my father asked me to deliver these furs to the inn in Bloodhoof.\nI'm far from rested enough to complete both my rite and this task for my father. Would you mind going on for me?\nThe inn is pleasant and a perfect place to rest during your long travels. I'm sure you'll agree once you see it.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Tough Hunk of Bread 5 Refreshing Spring Water\nExperience: 110\n+25 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Yes, young one? What can Kauth do for you?\nThe journey here from the Mesa can be a tremendous burden for some, but a welcome sight for others. Which is it for you, I wonder?","done":"Ah, the furs I was expecting. Thank you.\nThese came faster than I had expected. They will make good blankets for anyone who wishes to stay here.\nPlease feel free to stay as long as you like. My inn is always open and all of our people are welcome here. And don't underestimate a good night's rest, it can make a great difference while you're out traveling.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":39.2,"y":81.2,"n":"Antur Fallow","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":45.9,"y":64.2,"n":"Innkeeper Kauth","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"776":{"id":776,"t":"Rites of the Earthmother","lv":14,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff wants you to bring him the Horn of Arra'chea.\nHorn of Arra'chea Arra'chea","desc":"You have passed the Rites of the Earthmother and earned your place in Thunder Bluff.\nBut in order to maintain the spot that you strived so hard to achieve, you must continue to prove your worth to your people.\nWe are hunters, ‹name›. Down below in Mulgore there is a mighty kodo named Arra'chea. Show me your skills in the ways of tracking and hunting by bringing me the Horn of Arra'chea.","rew":"You will receive:\nKodo Hunter's Leggings\nExperience: 1,250\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you tracked down Arra'chea yet?","done":"Well done! A fine kill that was.\nI will send a gathering party to collect the carcass so we can retrieve the hide and meat.\nYou have done a great deed for your people, ‹name›.\nThunder Bluff Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":60.3,"y":51.7,"n":"Cairne Bloodhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9096":{"id":9096,"t":"Frostfire Leggings","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Frostfire Leggings if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Leggings, 20 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 4 Mooncloth and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Leggings\n20 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Mooncloth\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"As a Watcher, I was allowed access to many of Medivh's personal effects. Among those items, I found the tomes most enlightening. While the majority of the books were filled with - to put it bluntly - tripe, there were some gems. One of those tomes documented the creation of a set of armor fit for an archmage: Frostfire.\n<Angela points to her head.>\nIt's all in here and I am willing to share the fruits of that knowledge with you as long as you are able to provide me with the necessary materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostfire Leggings\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !,\nyou got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Frostfire Leggings.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"936":{"id":936,"t":"Assisting Arch Druid Runetotem","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"Excuse me ‹class›, but I'd like just a moment of your time if possible.\nThe Cenarion Circle in Thunder Bluff is most interested in seasoned adventurers such as yourself to lend them aid in a vital research project. While I do not know the specifics, I can inform you that none other than Hamuul Runetotem is spearheading this research.\nPlease - if you are interested, speak with him directly on the Elder Rise within Thunder Bluff proper.","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Greetings, ‹class›; I am glad you are interested in assisting our research. There is much to do, and I would be doing you a disservice if I informed you that the work this entails is not dangerous. Hopefully this will not scare you off... but from the looks of you, I take it that danger is something that you have dealt with before.\nOrgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":54.1,"y":68.4,"n":"Innkeeper Gryshka","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"9016":{"id":9016,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Wildheart Boots, a Wildheart Kilt and Wildheart Spaulders.\nWildheart Boots Mother Smolderweb 15 %\nWildheart Kilt Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nWildheart Spaulders Gizrul the Slavener 15 %\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together. Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nFeralheart Boots Feralheart Kilt Feralheart Spaulders\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, ‹name›. Let us take care of your reward first.","done":"This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.\nEastern Plaguelands Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"94776":{"id":94776,"t":"Divine grace","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.","desc":"Time's come for you to head to Stormwind, ‹name›. High Priestess Laurena in the Cathedral of Light wants to speak to you. Gotta be somethin' really good or really bad for the High Priestess to want you there personally, but I'm guessin' you've only done well for yourself and it's a good thing that she wants to speak to ya.\nBut don't waste too much time 'round here. I'd head there as soon as you can.\nLevel 10 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 13 16 Side Alliance Class Priest Shareable Yes Quest ID 94776","cats":["priest"]},"5656":{"id":5656,"t":"Hex of Weakness","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar.","desc":"It always warms my undying heart to see priests from all cultures wander the world. To know that power exists that is not arcane and well within our grasp. That's why it is my honor to direct you home, ‹name›.\nUr'kyo, your great priest in Orgrimmar, has asked for your presence. You can find him in the Valley of Spirits.","rew":"You will learn: Hex of Weakness\nExperience: 210","done":"You would do well to pay heed to this lesson, young one. The Hex of Weakness will be a great boon to you in battle. Later I will have tests for you to further yourself and prove your worth to the tribe.\nUndercity Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":49.1,"y":14.6,"n":"Father Lankester","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.6,"y":87.8,"n":"Ur'kyo","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"95816":{"id":95816,"t":"Sign me up","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the completed form to Elaine Compton in Redridge Mountains.\nAdvertising License Application\nMassive Pile of Completed Forms","desc":"Greetings, accomplished craftsperson!\nCompletion of this form will grant you non-exclusive, revocable, and legally limited permission to display advertisement signs for your tradeskill(s) all across Azeroth!\nOnce completed, please bring this to your local Azeroth Commerce Authority branch's Contract Coordinator to begin processing.\nHappy crafting!","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650\nStart an item: Advertising License Application Level 60 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 56 58 Side Both factions Quest ID 95816","cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"3096":{"id":3096,"t":"Encrypted Scroll","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Encrypted Scroll and speak to David Trias in Deathknell.\nEncrypted Scroll\nProvided: Encrypted Scroll","desc":"Ah, while you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. I would think it's some matter of importance as it seems it bears the seal of the rogue trainer David Trias. I would take some time to read it before heading out again.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"So you've made it? Good, we'll have need of more rogues as time goes on. The Shadowstalkers will probably wind up finding you when they think the time's right, so don't go and slip up or do anything you might regret. They need talented agents... not pickpockets and fools.","done":"I spend most of my time here in the inn keeping an eye out for new faces and just keeping tabs on up-and-coming prospects. Keep your nose clean and I'll do what I can to teach you a few things. Just come back to me whenever you want, and we'll see if you're ready for a new skill or two.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.8,"y":66.2,"n":"Shadow Priest Sarvis","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":32.5,"y":65.7,"n":"David Trias","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"7736":{"id":7736,"t":"Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Kingsblood","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 2 Incendosaur Scales, 4 Kingsblood and one Coal to Master Smith Burninate.\n2 Incendosaur Scale Incendosaur\n4 Kingsblood Kingsblood , Branch Snapper 3.8 % , Kurzen Medicine Man 3.7 % , Wandering Protector 3.6 % and 4 more\nCoal Dalaran Miner , Blazing Elemental 28.4 % , Inferno Elemental 24.7 % , Molten Giant 24.7 % and 4 more","desc":"Let's not waste more of my precious time with jibber jabber, ‹name›. It's time to focus on replenishing our dwindling fiery flux supply.\nWhat I'm gonna need from you is the following:\n*2 Incendosaur scales.\n*4 Kingsblood.\n*1 Coal.\nI'll take all that you can offer!\nAnd you'll do it fast if you wanna get in good with the Brotherhood.","back":"Let's not waste more of my precious time with jibber jabber, ‹race›. It's time to focus on replenishing our dwindling fiery flux supply.\nWhat I'm gonna need from you is the following:\n*Incendosaur scales.\n*Kingsblood.\n*Coal.\nI'll take all that you can offer!\nAnd you'll do it fast if you wanna get in good with the Brotherhood.","done":"There's always room for more fiery flux, junior. Keep it comin'... unless I tell you to stop.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":38.8,"y":28.5,"n":"Master Smith Burninate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"94616":{"id":94616,"t":"Water sapta","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","rew":"You will receive:\nWater Sapta","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":41.8,"y":19,"n":"Norric Lochthane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"96136":{"id":96136,"t":"Call of air","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles.","desc":"As you have no doubt experienced yourself, the elements of Azeroth are unique to those in Zephras. It is one thing to channel the forces of nature within the elemental plains, and another thing entirely to do it down here in the muck.\nI could grant you your totem of air, but I think it would do you more good to meet with the one who trains the other earth-bound initiates. What say you, ‹name›?","rew":"You will receive:\nAir Totem\nMoney: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Horde Shareable Yes Quest ID 96136","cats":["shaman"]},"8376":{"id":8376,"t":"Armaments of War","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Reservist's Legplates Crystal Lined Greaves\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"War comes, ‹name›, and with it comes untold horrors. You have done all that could be asked of you and for that you should be rewarded.\nShould this... this prophecy ever come to pass...\n<Geologist Larksbane turns pale.>\nThe future of us all could be at an end.\nThese armaments will prove invaluable to your campaign in this desert.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8536":{"id":8536,"t":"Earthen Templar","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Summon and slay an Earthen Templar and report back to Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold. You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing III in order to complete this quest.\nTactical Task Briefing III\nEarthen Templar slain\nProvided: Tactical Task Briefing III","desc":"The Twilight's Hammer and the elemental nobles they worship present a formidable threat to our operations in Silithus. With the new enemies we're facing inside Ahn'Qiraj, we cannot afford to lower our guard to our enemies outside.\nFind a way to summon and destroy an Earthen Templar and report to Bor Wildmane.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Tactical Badge Followup Tactical Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Is your task done yet, ‹name›?","done":"Good job, ‹name›. Here's your next assignment.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"9416":{"id":9416,"t":"Report to General Kirika","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 53.","obj":"Speak with General Kirika at the Horde encampment near Hive'Regal.","desc":"You must be one of General Kirika's new recruits. It's about time you showed up. Bodies wear down quick in the desert.\nThe dwarves have been getting reinforcements daily, and we can't afford to lose ground in our struggle for resources in Silithus.\nGet your instructions from the General. It's not my job to train you, just find you.","done":"It's good that you're here, but there's no time to waste making small talk. You need instructions, and then you need to get out there.\nListen up.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49,"y":36.7,"n":"Scout Bloodfist","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":50.8,"y":69.5,"n":"General Kirika","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8776":{"id":8776,"t":"Target: Hive'Regal Slavemakers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 30 Hive'Regal Slavemakers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Combat Task Briefing X in order to complete this quest.\nCombat Task Briefing X\nHive'Regal Slavemaker slain : 0/ 30\nProvided: Combat Task Briefing X","desc":"As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations. You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Regal where your primary target will consist of the Hive'Regal slavemakers.\nReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Combat Badge\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You wish to tell me something, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. Your part in the attack on Hive'Regal has been noted.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8856":{"id":8856,"t":"Desert Survival Kits","min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Globes of Water, 4 Powerful Anti-Venom and 4 Baked Salmon to Calandrath at the inn in Cenarion Hold in Silithus.\n4 Globe of Water Princess Tempestria 77.1 % , Lord Skwol 47.6 % , Hydrospawn 20 % , Muck Splash 16.1 % and 4 more\n4 Powerful Anti-Venom\n4 Smoked Desert Dumplings\nLogistics Task Briefing I\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing I","desc":"With the arrival of fresh recruits to Cenarion Hold comes the problem of keeping them alive in the desert. Dehydration as well as numerous poisonous creatures present a serious threat to inexperienced volunteers. Gather the supplies necessary for a desert survival kit and bring them to Calandrath in Cenarion Hold.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Followup Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle\nLevel 0 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Shareable No Quest ID 8856","cats":["silithus"]},"1096":{"id":1096,"t":"Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle","lv":27,"min":16,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle's Mechanical Arm to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.\nGerenzo's Mechanical Arm Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle","desc":"I met Gerenzo once, but let me tell you, he's not easy on the eyes. His flesh looks like it's rotting away, and he's grafted metal and gears onto his body, replaced some of his limbs with mechanical ones.\nNortheast of here, far above Cragpool Lake, up near the water wheel is where Gerenzo watches over the entire site. There's no way I could fight my way up there, not to mention take on Gerenzo... But you look like you might be able to make it.\nIf you kill him for me, I'll make it worth your while!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEngineer's Cloak Draftsman Boots\nMoney: 22 0 gold, 22 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,200\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Sputtervalve will want some sort of proof that Gerenzo's dead. I think his mechanical arm will probably do.","done":"Look at that thing... it'd take a gnome to come up with something like that. I can't understand why you'd cut off an arm, and replace it with that, when you could just keep both arms and add a third!\nGnomes, I tell you...\nAt least Gerenzo's out of commission. Hopefully that'll be enough proof, and Sputtervalve will assign me to one of the Tinkers' Union workshops in Gadgetzan or maybe even Undermine.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59,"y":62.6,"n":"Ziz Fizziks","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"7496":{"id":7496,"t":"Celebrating Good Times","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Major Mattingly in the Valley of Heroes.","desc":"Seek out Major Mattingly in the Valley of Heroes, ‹name›. He will be expecting you...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOnyxia Blood Talisman Dragonslayer's Signet Onyxia Tooth Pendant\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Few are graced with such ceremony, ‹name›. Please, choose your reward so that we may begin the celebration.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":67.2,"y":85.5,"n":"Major Mattingly","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"616":{"id":616,"t":"The Haunted Isle","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay.","desc":"Baron Revilgaz has had me keep an ear out for rumors of the strange and out-of-place in Booty Bay and Stranglethorn. I don't usually put much stock in ghost stories, but I heard some sailors in the tavern talking about a haunted island off the coast. Water elementals and a raving goblin ghost, they say.\nIf you're going to go talk to Revilgaz, could you relay that story to him?","rew":"Experience: 290","done":"Interesting. Some time ago, I seem to remember reading a book once that suggested...\nAh, of course, a troll legend it was. If what Krazek reports is true, perhaps I will soon be able to add the Stone of the Tides to my collection of ancient artifacts and relics.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":77.2,"n":"Krazek","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":76.9,"n":"Baron Revilgaz","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8056":{"id":8056,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Augur's Bracers","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Maywiki of Zuldazar a Primal Hakkari Armsplint. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.\nMaywiki of Zuldazar is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Armsplint\nReach 3000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"The augurs of our tribe are revered for their gifts of the divine sight, ya mon. They ain't a witch doctor; they spend their time castin' bones or readin' the leaves for insight - not hexin' people. As a shaman, you already know somethin' about the power of augury; we Zandalar prize the insight they give to the tribe.\nBring me an offerin' of the Paragons of Power from inside Zul'Gurub and prove your worth to us. Do this for us, and I'll give ya some bracers that our augurs prize above all others!","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Augur's Bracers\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Got the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub that I need? These bracers are well worth any effort ya be needin' to make!","done":"It seems ya got a bit of the Zandalar augur in ya. We know about the deeds you've been doin' in Zul'Gurub on our behalf mon. These Paragons of Power will go a long way to helpin' out the Zandalar tribe - a tribe, I might add, ya can call upon as friends. Take these bracers, ‹name›; ya earned them and then some!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"93176":{"id":93176,"t":"My little friends","lv":35,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the items contained in the Entomology Starter Kit to find and catch an Arbor Tarantula, Hay Weevil Specimen, and a Flesh Picker.\nArbor Tarantula Specimen\nHay Weevil Specimen\nFlesh Picker Specimen","desc":"Admiring my little menagerie, are you? They are my un-life's work. I've spent countless hours studying them: their anatomy, their diets, even their social rituals.\nDo you wish to join me in the hobby? Here, take this package. The notes and materials contained within should get you started. If you lose it, you'll have to purchase another one from me for a small fee.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":25,"y":54.2,"n":"Amaryllis Webb","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"456":{"id":456,"t":"The Balance of Nature","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 7 Young Nightsabers and 4 Young Thistle Boars and return to Conservator Ilthalaine.\nYoung Nightsaber slain : 0/ 7\nYoung Thistle Boar slain : 0/ 4","desc":"Greetings, ‹name›. I am Conservator Ilthalaine. My purpose in Shadowglen is to ensure that the balance of nature is maintained.\nThe spring rains were particularly heavy this year, causing some of the forest's beasts to flourish while others suffered.\nUnfortunately, the nightsaber and thistle boar populations grew too large. Shadowglen can only produce so much food for the beasts. Journey forth, young ‹class›, and thin the boar and saber populations so that nature's harmony will be preserved.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nArchery Training Gloves Stemleaf Bracers\nMoney: 35 0 gold, 0 silver, 35 copper Experience: 170\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"There is still work to be done, ‹name›. Return to me once you have thinned the nightsaber and thistle boar populations.","done":"You performed your duties well, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.7,"y":44.3,"n":"Conservator Ilthalaine","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"7816":{"id":7816,"t":"Gammerita, Mon!","lv":48,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Katoom the Angler at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to kill Gammerita and retrieve Katoom's Best Lure from her corpse.\nKatoom mentioned that Gammerita hangs out on the coast with the other turtles.\nKatoom's Best Lure Gammerita","desc":"Yo! There be a turtle out there not like the others. She be the Gammerita, leader of the saltwater snapjaws - a downright dirty thievin' reptile.\nMon, she stole my best lure. Snapped it right off my line! Since then, the fish just aren't biting the same.\nFind Gammerita and get my lure out of her stomach.","rew":"Money: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"Did you get it yet?","done":"MON! This is fantastic! With my best lure and the snapjaw population down, the fish will pile up.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":80.3,"y":81.5,"n":"Katoom the Angler","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"79976":{"id":79976,"t":"This must be the place","lv":32,"min":14,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Whoever was here, you just missed them.","desc":"\"So, I've decided to take my work back underground. To stop it falling into the wrong hands.\"\n<The paper is torn just large enough to fit the message. You aren't sure if these are the last words you'll read from the author, or if they're a clue to the next hideout. An inadequately secured sleeping bag is unrolling itself onto your feet...>","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211527 Item 216619\nExperience: 1,950","done":"Heavy canvas is rolled over assorted equipment. You help yourself to the pack.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":22.5,"y":24.2,"n":"Messenger Bag","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":22.5,"y":24.2,"n":"Hastily Rolled-Up Satchel","e":1}],"cats":["thoradins-wall"]},"1176":{"id":1176,"t":"Load Lightening","lv":30,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get 10 Hollow Vulture Bones for Pozzik in the Shimmering Flats.\n10 Hollow Vulture Bone Salt Flats Scavenger , Salt Flats Vulture","desc":"When it comes to racing, every bit counts! Whether it's a minor tweaking on the power output, a slight slackening on the tension coils, or lightening the weight of the frame, you have to take everything into account.\nWe use vulture bones for a lot of the minor structural tweaks we make to our racers, which offer the perfect balance of strength and weight. Even better, it's easy for us to get more, as the salt flats are littered with vultures.\nBring me some and I'll give you a good price on them.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,850\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Do you have those bones for me? I was just about to start working on lightening the steering rig, but I don't want to open her up without all the parts I need.","done":"Great! I can get the crew working on this right away. Thanks, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":80.2,"y":75.9,"n":"Pozzik","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"376":{"id":376,"t":"The Damned","lv":2,"min":2,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Novice Elreth requires 6 Scavenger Paws and 6 Duskbat Wings.\n6 Scavenger Paw Ragged Scavenger 75 % , Young Scavenger 75 %\n6 Duskbat Wing Mangy Duskbat 75 % , Duskbat 75 %","desc":"My duties include tending to our wounded warriors, tailoring armor and clothes, and assisting Shadow Priest Sarvis with whatever else he might need.\nFrom the look of it, you'll be enlisted in his service also... hunting the Mindless Ones, if I know his mind. Well, if you'd like to stay in one piece--and I've no doubt you do--perhaps I can help. I'm running out of paws and wings, and if you bring me some, I'll find some armor for you. You'll find a good number of wolves and bats to the south.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFlax Bracers Old Leather Belt\nExperience: 170\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do try your best to keep yourself unharmed until I get you some armor.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. This armor should help you out.\nHopefully, it should do you more good than the last one to wear it...","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.9,"y":66.1,"n":"Novice Elreth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"5096":{"id":5096,"t":"Scarlet Diversions","lv":53,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Proceed to the Scarlet Crusade's base camp between Felstone Field and Dalson's Tears and destroy their command tent.\nPlace the Scourge banner at the camp, and then return to High Executor Derrington at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\nProvided: Scourge Banner","desc":"Before Andorhal, we must tackle the advancing Scarlet Crusade menace from Hearthglen. They've made camp between Felstone Field and Dalson's Tears, making us risk conflict against both the Scourge and the Crusade at once.\nMy plan is to play them off of each other by sending you to destroy the command tent they've set up; use some Flame in a Bottle from this box of incendiaries. Once razed, plant this Scourge banner by the tent. With some luck, they'll ignore us and focus on the Scourge for vengeance.","rew":"Money: 80 0 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,250\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"A surprise raid on the Scarlet Crusade's tenuous forward position will give us a buffer of time to be able to march on Andorhal. I trust you are here to report success!\nOnce this is successfully executed, we will need to work diligently and quickly. We do not have the materiel and manpower to fight both the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade at the same time if they do not buy our little ruse.","done":"Finely executed, ‹name›. Your attack on the Scarlet Crusade will buy us time. I have sent one of my best scouts out to watch over the camp and make sure that the Crusade forces that come to reinforce the position will take the bait.\nWith the pressure on us lessened, we should now finally be able to risk a mission into Andorhal itself, and an important one at that. I'd very much like it if you'd perform this one as well, based on your success to date.\nTirisfal Glades Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.1,"y":68.9,"n":"High Executor Derrington","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"136":{"id":136,"t":"Captain Sander's Hidden Treasure","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Captain Sanders' footlocker and search it for the next clue.","desc":"If ye be readin' this, it means that Ol' Captain Sanders is in a watery grave. So my treasure is yours now, ye jest need to follow the clues.\nFirst ye need to find me footlocker. It's probably half-buried in sand by now, along the Western Coast of Westfall near the shipwreck. There be lots of shipwrecks but only one rusty anchor on the coast. Find that anchor and you'll find me locker! Look in there for the next clue.","rew":"Experience: 575","done":"The footlocker slowly creaks open. Sand and water seem to be its only contents. But wait! A small crab scurries out with a clue to the treasure in his claws!","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":25.9,"y":47.8,"n":"Captain's Footlocker","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"296":{"id":296,"t":"Ormer's Revenge","lv":29,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Raptorclaw Shoulders.","obj":"Ormer Ironbraid at the Whelgar Excavation Site wants you to kill Sarltooth and return to him with one of his talons once the task is fulfilled.\nSarltooth's Talon Sarltooth","desc":"While you were down there I happened to notice that one of those beasts stood out from the rest. He was bigger and more menacing. I bet he's the one who led the others here to cause the disruption to the dig site.\nI ask of you now one final task, ‹name›. See to it that Sarltooth is brought to justice. And considering the gravity of his crimes, justice in this case means death! Bring me one of his talons as proof of his death.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRaptor's End Raptorbane Armor Excavation Rod Raptorclaw Shoulders\nNew in Forever: Raptorclaw Shoulders.\nYou will also receive:\nRecipe: Curiously Tasty Omelet\nExperience: 2,950\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Is Sarltooth dead? Have you redeemed the memory of the fallen?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Your efforts here will not be forgotten. Many innocent Dwarves died at this site, simply doing their jobs. The vengeance you delivered to those evil creatures should make them think twice before attacking King Magni's subjects ever again.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":38.2,"y":50.9,"n":"Ormer Ironbraid","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"98216":{"id":98216,"t":"Understanding our present","lv":31,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Goaz Stone near the Goaz Warder and bring its Titanic Keystone back to Prospector Whelgar.\nTitanic Keystone","desc":"Old Gods?! This cannot be good news at all!\nI've made out a new bit on the stone that speaks of a guardian of some kind. Whatever it is, it must be linked to the stone!\nTake it with you and see if you can find a big Titan construct of some sort in the excavation. Read this here final passage on the stone and see what happens!\nIf I'm right, you'll activate the thing. Take it out if so, but try to preserve anything interesting! We simply must know more!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nProspector's Signet Excavation Cloak\nExperience: 3,150","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":38.8,"y":52.2,"n":"Prospector Whelgar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"93736":{"id":93736,"t":"Unwelcome spirits","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 10 Wind Hollow Essences from Wind Hollows in the Shadowgale Forest.\n10 Wind Hollow Essence","desc":"The paramount concern of the Windshapers is to better understand why the spirits left us, and what we may be able to do to bring them back. One curious fixture of Shadowgale Forest to the north is the presence of a curious form of wind sprite that some call \"hollows\". We know little of them and why they are there, but we do know that they first started to appear after the spirits of the wind left us.\nI need you to go there and disperse them. Gather the remains and bring them back here.","back":"Shadowgale Forest is a dangerous place. Some even say its haunted. I'm quite sure that I don't believe that, but I do know that its not for the faint hearted, or the unprepared.","done":"Handling these essences fills me with a sense of... deep disquiet. I can almost feel a malevolent, regretful aura emanating from them. It's enough to make me faint.\n<Endaria shudders slightly.>\nI do not look forward to studying these further.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":58.2,"y":78.4,"n":"Endaria Mistgaze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"2936":{"id":2936,"t":"The Spider God","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read from the Tablet of Theka to learn the name of the Witherbark spider god, then return to Master Gadrin.","desc":"The Witherbarks worship a spider god, and from her they collect their most potent venom. So if you want the venom, then you must summon their god!\nTo do that, you must know her true name, and that name is on a tablet buried in Tanaris, in the troll city of Zul'Farrak, in a tomb guarded by Theka the Martyr.\nDefeat Theka and find and read his tablet to discover the spider god's name. When you know it, return to me.","rew":"Experience: 4,850\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Do you know the spider god's name?","done":"Ah, Elortha no Shadra... speak this name only in whispers, for its utterance carries much weight in the realms of the spirit.\nI will put it to parchment and create for you a spell of summoning...\nDurotar Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":55.9,"y":74.7,"n":"Master Gadrin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulfarrak"]}});